# Known divergence (by design): single-variant topology test helpers run a dynamic
# EXECUTE the gateway cannot vet, so their CREATE is rejected. The helpers are
# re-seeded per test (postgis_preseed.sql) so the checks run; only the rejected
# CREATEs remain. With format()-argument analysis, three of the rejected bodies now
# fail skeleton reconstruction ("could not be parsed") and one stays a plain
# runtime-built rejection.
--- a
+++ b
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+ERROR: a dynamic EXECUTE statement inside a PL/pgSQL body could not be parsed for safety analysis
+ERROR: a dynamic EXECUTE statement inside a PL/pgSQL body could not be parsed for safety analysis
+ERROR: a dynamic EXECUTE statement inside a PL/pgSQL body could not be parsed for safety analysis
+ERROR: EXECUTE of a runtime-built statement inside a PL/pgSQL body is not supported: the statement text is not a constant, so it cannot be checked for unsafe session-state changes
 ERROR: SQL/MM Spatial exception - null argument
